Privacy Policy for DevOps PocketKit
Last Updated: February 10, 2026


DevOps PocketKit ("the Application") is designed with a strict 100% Offline & Zero Data Collection Policy. Your privacy, infrastructure configurations, credentials, and notes are completely protected because the Application operates entirely offline without network access.


1. Zero Network Access & Permission Policy
• The Application does not include the android.permission.INTERNET permission in its Android Manifest.
• The Application cannot connect to any external server, cloud service, telemetry provider, or analytics platform.
• All calculations, token decodings, manifest generations, regex evaluations, and search queries take place purely on your physical device.

2. Information Collection and Use
• Personal Data: The Application does not collect, store, transmit, or share any personally identifiable information (PII).
• Device Information: The Application does not track hardware IDs, IP addresses, location data, or device identifiers.
• Analytics & Tracking: The Application contains zero third-party SDKs, tracking pixels, or analytics trackers.

3. Local Storage & Encryption at Rest
• Any scratchpad notes or snippets created within the Application are stored locally in an encrypted database on your device using hardware-backed AES-256-GCM authenticated encryption (AndroidKeyStore).
• Data stored by the Application is excluded from cloud device backups (android:allowBackup="false").

4. Third-Party Access
Because the Application does not collect or transmit any data, no third parties have access to your data under any circumstances.

5. Contact Us
If you have any questions regarding this Privacy Policy, please contact @ rselvaguru@gmail.com.
